<title>UK: Granada drops as Robinson cuts stake.</title>
<headline>Granada drops as Robinson cuts stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Granada Group Plc dropped on Monday after chairman Gerry Robinson sold 57,500 shares in the media-to-hotels group, cutting his stake to 300,872 shares.</p>
<p>Granada shares were down 17-1/2p at 895 by 1558 GMT in heavy trading of 3.7 million shares.  </p>
<p>In a formal statement to the Stock Exchange, Granada said Robinson had sold the shares at 914p, a deal that would have realised over half a million pounds. It gave no reason for the sale. Dealers said the stock had also been hit today by profit-taking following its recent strong gains. Granada hit a record 924p on February 4.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
